These wav files customize FreeSWITCH conference prompts under
`en/us/callie/conference/`:

## Mute / unmute (SafeMeet)

Mute and unmute alerts are played by the HTML5 client from:

- `bigbluebutton-html5/public/resources/sounds/conf-muted.mp3`
- `bigbluebutton-html5/public/resources/sounds/conf-unmuted.mp3`

FreeSWITCH `muted-sound` / `unmuted-sound` are disabled in
`bbb-voice-conference/.../conference.conf.xml` (and re-applied on package
install by `bbb-freeswitch-core` after-install) so those English conference
wavs are not mixed into the voice channel.

The short `conf-muted.wav` / `conf-unmuted.wav` files under `48000/` remain
available as optional FreeSWITCH overrides if an admin re-enables those
params manually.

## Alone in conference

- `conf-alone.wav` — SafeMeet prompt when you are alone in the conference
  (replaces the English FreeSWITCH default; shipped at
  8000 / 16000 / 32000 / 48000 Hz)

Package builds install `conf-alone.wav` via `bbb-freeswitch-sounds`.

For a live server that already has FreeSWITCH sounds installed, you can also
apply the overrides with:

```
cp -r /etc/bigbluebutton/bbb-conf/sounds /opt/freeswitch/share/freeswitch
```

(after packaging/copying this directory to `/etc/bigbluebutton/bbb-conf/sounds`).
